1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,480
Right, that's all for today's class.

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,560
Remember, college entrance exams are next year,

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,300
so studying will eat up most of your summer break.

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:16,200
I encourage you to go out and enjoy the pool or beach while you still can.

5
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:19,880
In fact, I'd be happy to come with you.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:20,800
What?

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,960
Why the hell would we invite a teacher to tag along?

8
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,820
Don't be dense, Ishikawa.

9
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:29,580
If there are swimsuits involved, you're going to need adult supervision.

10
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,600
Oh, yeah, that makes sense.

11
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,680
Their stupidity is baffling.

12
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:41,440
Yasuda would be a certified hottie if he didn't talk.

13
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:43,500
Maybe, but at least he's a good teacher.

14
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,040
Just ignore the dumb things he says.

15
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:50,500
Ori, did something happen between the two of you?

16
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,040
This morning.

17
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,840
Hey, Ori. Keep your chin up.

18
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:58,360
Okay. Random.

19
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,480
Not random if you knew how much I love flat-chested girls.

20
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,660
Flat-chested girls are A-OK.

21
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:06,420
He thought that would cheer me up.

22
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:09,480
Wow. Just what goes on in his head.

23
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,280
Oh, yeah. So, Ori.

24
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:11,780
Hmm?

25
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:15,980
This guy from another school was asking me for your phone number the other day.

26
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:17,860
Can I give it to him?

27
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:21,080
He didn't have the guts to ask me himself, so thanks.

28
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,180
But no thanks.

29
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:23,580
Oh, what? Again?

30
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:26,400
Yo. Who's up for some bad singing?

31
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:27,640
Like today?

32
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:30,240
Since these coupons expire today, yeah.

33
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,560
Half of two hours? What a steal!

34
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,360
You want to go? Come on.

35
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,120
It'll be fun.

36
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:39,280
Uh, I think I'm gonna pass.

37
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,420
Ori, you always pass.

38
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:44,200
I know. I'm sorry.

39
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:47,680
Excuse me.

40
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:48,360
Huh?

41
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:50,880
Here you go.

42
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:52,420
You dropped this.

43
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,160
Thanks. I didn't notice.

44
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,780
He sounded so depressed.

45
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:00,900
Then again, that's kind of his thing.

46
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:02,900
I bet he's a total otaku.

47
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,940
This angle's death, my favorite.

48
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:08,760
Like, into Moe?

49
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,140
A hundred percent.

50
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,040
He has to be.

51
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,560
Does your nerd alert pick up anything?

52
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:14,560
Hmm.

53
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:17,200
That dude is one giant mystery to me.

54
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,920
I don't even know if Miyamura has friends.

55
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,440
Sorry!

56
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,440
Gotta run!

57
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,240
And there she goes.

58
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,580
It feels like she hurries home every day.

59
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:30,000
Must be a boyfriend or something.

60
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:30,840
You serious?

61
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:33,900
Well, she's way popular.

62
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:35,540
It's not that surprising.

63
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,080
You're right!

64
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,500
Hey, Mom.

65
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,600
Got it.

66
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,180
I'll handle dinner.

67
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:58,860
Overtime sucks, I know.

68
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:00,300
Bye.

69
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,300
I should probably get going.

70
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:06,200
Sota!

71
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:08,460
Hey, Sissy!

72
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,200
We've been waiting for you.

73
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:16,500
I know!

74
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,800
Let's hit up that store we saw in that magazine over here.

75
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,620
Wait, right now?

76
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,440
Why not?

77
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:22,500
Yeah, why not?

78
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,320
I'm thinking hamburgers for dinner.

79
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:24,780
Yummy!

80
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:25,620
Goo-B!

81
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:33,080
Yay!

82
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,720
Bye.

83
