Empty

104
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:29,040
Thank you!

105
00:04:47,260 --> 00:05:02,040
Overtime and working on her day off.

106
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:06,180
I swear, she's too nice for her own good.

107
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:09,000
I wish she'd learn how to say no to people.

108
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:10,800
Sufi?

109
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:12,600
Yeah?

110
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,500
Are you okay?

111
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:19,260
Sota!

112
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,240
What happened to your little nose?

113
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,500
I fell down.

114
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,560
Where's your handkerchief, buddy?

115
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,620
So, uh...

116
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:27,820
Huh?

117
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:31,360
I'm gonna go since you've got it taken care of.

118
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:33,140
I didn't even see him there!

119
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,140
Ah, sorry.

120
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:37,180
Hope he didn't cause you too much trouble.

121
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:38,180
That's fine.

122
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,720
Anyway, I'll see you later.

123
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,040
Sota?

124
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,060
Uh, you good?

125
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:49,360
You know, if you're not in any sort of hurry, you're more than welcome to stay for a while.

126
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:52,120
Oh, I don't know. You sure?

127
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:55,080
This will be my way of saying thanks. So yeah.

128
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,980
He fell down because this dog spooked him.

129
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:00,940
I appreciate you helping him out.

130
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,100
And I appreciate you for treating me.

131
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:06,740
Um, hey bro, why do you drink coffee if it tastes so gross?

132
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:08,620
I ask myself the same thing.

133
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:10,420
Your brother's a good kid.

134
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,720
He introduced himself in everything.

135
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,560
Thanks. That's nice of you to say.

136
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,520
He's a real handful most of the time.

137
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:20,820
Although, taking care of him and all the housework is what's really impressive.

138
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,100
Never would have guessed, Hori.

139
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:22,800
Yeah.

140
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:28,460
What's wrong? I mean, you are Hori, right? From class one?

141
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,780
Well, I mean, I am. But how'd you know that?

142
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:34,780
Do you go to the same school as me?

143
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:37,200
What? Are you being serious right now?

144
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,440
I'm Miyamura and we're in the same class.

145
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,000
Wait.

146
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:43,180
What?

147
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:49,780
That can't be the same person.

148
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:52,480
If they are, the world doesn't make sense anymore.

149
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:55,760
You're making one of the weirdest faces in the history of weird faces.

150
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:56,660
What's up?

151
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,140
Nothing's up.

152
00:06:59,080 --> 00:06:59,900
Are you sure?

153
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:05,000
Where are you going?

154
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:05,800
Hori!

155
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,640
Miyamura, got a sec?

156
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:10,840
What?

157
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:13,660
You're asking me to come over to your house again?

158
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:16,940
I'm not asking for me. I'm asking for my little brother, Sota.

159
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:20,080
He wants that cool dude that saved him from the dog to come play a while.

160
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:23,800
Really? Then I'll pick up a picture book for him or something.

161
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,780
It's fine. Just showing up will be enough, trust me.

162
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:31,560
What a relief. Now I don't have to break Sota's heart.

163
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:35,080
I'm kinda shocked.

164
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:35,940
By what?

165
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:39,620
By the fact that you sought me out and are talking to me.

166
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,940
After yesterday and all.

167
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:42,140
Well, you know.

168
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,520
I thought for sure you'd avoid me.

169
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,960
You really think I'd react that way?

170
00:07:47,260 --> 00:07:50,980
I'm not gonna lie and say it wasn't awkward, because we both know it was.

171
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:53,520
It freaked me out to see such a different side of you.

172
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:58,920
But I'm different out of school too, so that'd be a pretty silly reason to straight up avoid you.

173
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:02,080
Why are you blushing?

174
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:05,240
I'm just not used to hearing stuff like this.

175
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:07,040
It feels kinda strange is all.

176
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,360
Still, thank you.

177
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:13,840
What's with the look?

178
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:15,760
I just noticed how nice your smile is.

179
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:16,300
Huh?

180
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:18,100
You should wear your hair up more often.

181
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,460
Maybe lose the glasses too.

182
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:20,360
Don't you think?

183
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:24,280
But then they'd see all the piercings that I have.

184
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:25,760
You do have quite a few.

185
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,860
So what's the grand total?

186
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:28,700
It's up to nine.

187
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:31,000
Four on each year along with the one on my lip.

188
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,160
That is way too many.

189
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:35,000
My mom would agree with you.

190
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:40,280
Here are some things I've learned about Miyamura since he started coming over.

191
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:43,600
I like manga, but I'm not into that moe nonsense.

192
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:44,980
He is not an otaku.

193
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,300
Brought some cake for you guys.

194
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:49,300
His family runs a cake shop.

195
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:50,640
Oh yeah.

196
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:53,400
That little hole hurt like you wouldn't believe.

197
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,060
He pierced himself with a safety pin back in middle school.

198
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,000
Also...

199
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,380
He's not a very good student.

200
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:05,880
Unbelievable, honey.

201
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,520
You're like a straight-A queen.

202
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:08,740
I'm really not.

203
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:12,100
What's incredible is how a quiet guy with glasses isn't smart.

204
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,520
Is that the rule?

205
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:18,600
It's times like these when I realize my initial impression of him

206
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:21,400
couldn't have been further from the person he actually is.

207
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,480
Isn't that a supermarket ad you got?

208
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:24,440
Yeah.

209
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:27,380
Eggs are on sale tomorrow, so...

210
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:29,440
Wow.

211
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:31,940
His bottom eyelashes are really long.

212
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:33,800
What's wrong?

213
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:34,540
Oh!

214
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:39,360
It's just, there's a sale on eggs tomorrow with no purchase limit.

215
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,960
But it says it only lasts till 4 p.m.

216
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,340
I've got this.

217
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,580
Nothing's gonna stand in my way.

218
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:48,140
Unless there's a committee meeting, but what are the odds?

219
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:53,740
All committee members, please report to the AZ room.

220
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:55,700
You're being called for an emergency meeting.

221
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:58,160
I guess the odds are pretty good.

222
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,840
But I'm not giving up on those eggs.

223
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:02,800
I refuse!

224
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,280
Where's the fire, Hori?

225
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:09,880
She's leaving it up to me!

226
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:17,580
Can't believe I'm running in the seat.

227
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:19,760
20 minutes to go.

228
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:21,680
I know a shortcut.

229
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:21,820
I know a shortcut.

230
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:42,180
Egg time!

231
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:43,200
I gotta go!

232
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:43,840
Huh?

233
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:45,620
What the heck?

234
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:48,840
Wait, what's egg time?

235
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:52,320
Man, I owe you one.

236
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,720
Uh, rabbit housewives everywhere.

237
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:59,180
I never want to see another sale as long as I live.

238
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,740
Oh yeah, I almost forgot.

239
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:05,760
I, uh, kinda sorta ran into somebody on my way there.

240
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:07,920
Kinda sorta?

241
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:08,860
Who was it?

242
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:11,200
That Yuki girl you hang out with.

243
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:12,400
Oh.

244
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:15,400
And she saw you...

245
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,940
looking like this?

246
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:19,720
Yeah, pretty sure she didn't recognize me though.

247
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:20,280
Surprise.

248
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:21,160
Uh-huh.

249
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,080
It's time to dig in!

250
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,760
Be careful not to spill.

251
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:27,500
Okay.

252
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:32,040
Miyamura, I can't explain exactly why,

253
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,320
but I don't want anybody else to see you this way.

254
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:36,160
Pretty selfish, huh?

255
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:39,720
Sorry!

256
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,020
What am I saying?

257
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:43,100
Forget it.

258
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:44,900
I'll get us some drinks.

259
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:46,280
Is barley tea okay?

260
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,140
Go ahead and eat.

261
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,420
It's yummy or hot.

262
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:52,560
You know what?

263
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:54,860
Um, me too.

264
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,920
I like seeing you outside of school.

265
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,300
Cooking dinner, getting mad and yelling

266
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,500
so everyone within a five-mile radius hears.

267
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:04,140
I even like the fact that you don't worry

268
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,320
about your appearance at home

269
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:07,680
and how you could probably suplex a truck.

270
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,340
I get the picture!

271
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:10,100
All I'm saying is,

272
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:12,680
I don't want anyone else to see this side of you either.

273
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:14,600
And no one will if I can help it.

274
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,020
It's nice.

275
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:19,260
It feels as if these moments are mine and mine alone.

276
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:26,660
I told you to stop talking ten seconds ago!

277
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,960
Now you're so close, please.

278
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,940
You're the best!

279
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:36,820
Jeez, how can you spout off about such cringey stuff

280
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:37,680
with a straight face?

281
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:40,280
I know his grades suck, but is he an idiot?

282
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:41,700
You dummy.

283
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,280
You're worse than a dummy.

284
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:46,140
You're like a dummy king.

285
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:47,500
King of the dummies.

286
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:48,940
If she says the word dummy,

287
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:51,120
she'll say it at least a hundred more times.

288
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:52,040
Are you joking?

289
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:56,340
Dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy, dummy.

290
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:57,060
I guess she does.

291
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,480
What's so funny?!

292
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:02,240
Everyone has a side that they prefer to keep to themselves.

293
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:03,800
Listen, Hori.

294
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,560
It's not that I don't like the way you are at school.

295
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,700
I just like this plainer and angrier version better.

296
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:12,440
I think it's a much cuter version of you.

297
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:15,100
Somehow, the two of us wound up sharing

298
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,740
our secret selves with one another.

299
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,620
Whatever, king dummy.

300
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:30,160
It's only going to get hotter, isn't it?

301
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:31,060
Yep.

302
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,240
Wearing this jacket all the time is going to be torture.

303
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:36,920
Yeah, but it could be worse, you know.

304
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,380
I'm screwed!

305
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:40,180
Mega screwed!

306
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,060
We're going to be swimming in B.E.

307
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,500
What should I do?!

308
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,140
You should suck it up and swim.

309
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:46,880
It's better than running a marathon,

310
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,440
especially when it's scorching.

311
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:50,320
Swimming is way worse.

312
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:52,340
It means they're going to see everything.

313
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,500
What are you talking about?

314
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:56,860
I'm talking about these!

315
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:03,400
There's a fine line between being bold and stupid.

316
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:06,680
Sometimes I'm not sure where you land.

317
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,680
At least swimming wound up being optional, huh?

318
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:11,980
Yeah, for real.

319
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:14,800
But if we have to run a marathon like you said,

320
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:17,420
I'll probably die of heatstroke because of this stupid jacket.

321
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:19,900
I don't actually think they'll make us do that, though.

322
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,200
Knowing my luck, we will.

323
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:23,440
Wow.

324
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:26,300
I never pictured those two spending so much time together.

325
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,800
Understatement of the year.

326
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:29,940
Yo, Hori!

327
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:32,060
You mind if I borrow your notes?

328
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,880
Oh, me too, me too!

329
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:34,760
Fine!

330
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:37,000
But you guys need to start taking your own.

331
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,440
I know, I know.

332
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:40,060
Thanks a bunch for this time, though.

333
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:42,860
She's popular.

334
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:44,460
Who?

335
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:46,280
You mean...

336
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:46,620
Hori?

337
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,240
Of course.

338
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:49,940
Uh...

339
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:50,600
Yeah.

340
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:53,720
I think that tends to happen when you have good grades.

341
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:54,960
Let's cut to the chase.

342
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:55,460
The chase?

343
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:57,020
Um, what chase?

344
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,080
You and Hori are tight these days.

345
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:01,260
Are you two a thing?

346
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:02,500
No!

347
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,340
What gave you that idea?

348
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,640
I thought as much.

349
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:11,240
I mean, you don't exactly have a lot in common.

350
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:12,200
Yeah.

351
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:12,920
True.

352
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:14,200
Very true.

353
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,360
We wouldn't make a good match in the slightest.

354
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,960
Um, we'd be...

355
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,920
Uh, uh, well...

356
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,100
Use your words, dude.

357
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:23,940
Don't see them together often.

358
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:25,020
Come on!

359
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:25,900
Let's get going!

360
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:27,700
I'm sorry.

361
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:29,700
Oh...

362
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,220
What?

363
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:31,760
I get it now.

364
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,620
Bet you have a crush on Hori, huh?

365
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:34,700
Ah!

366
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:38,460
Yeah, so what if I do?

367
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:39,400
Oh!

368
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:41,340
I thought you were gonna say no!

369
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:42,060
But!

370
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:42,880
Huh!

371
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:46,720
But that explains why you're always glaring at me when I'm talking to her!

372
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:48,160
Well, now you know!

373
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,340
Good for you!

374
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,660
I'm so sorry, Ishikawa.

375
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:54,780
I would have been more considerate had I known how much you like Hori!

376
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,140
I'm now to just the whole school!

377
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,060
Ah, my bad!

378
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:59,220
I guess I didn't realize it's still a secret!

379
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:00,480
Hey!

380
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:02,100
What are you two slackers doing?

381
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:03,560
P.E.'s about to start!

382
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:04,140
Ah!

383
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:09,120
We're already gonna be late, so we might as well take our time.

384
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:14,360
Uh, come to think of it, now that we're getting to know each other, why do you wear your winter

385
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,260
uniform in the summer?

386
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:16,200
Don't you get hot?

387
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,260
Um, actually...

388
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,260
I get cold?

389
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:20,840
You're sweating buckets, man.

390
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:25,540
Look, what I'm about to tell you might sound a little on the strange side.

391
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:26,880
Keep an open mind if you can.

392
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:29,740
Hori's the only person who's seen me without a shirt on.

393
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:30,540
Really?

394
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:31,500
Why?

395
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:36,040
So, if I show you, you have to promise you won't tell our teachers...

396
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,360
The last thing I am is a snitch!

397
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:41,160
It'd be a real pain if they found out, but I feel like I can trust you.

398
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,480
Ta-da!

399
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:45,340
Are those things real?

400
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:47,760
You're only a teenager and you've gotten that much ink done?

401
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:48,620
Yeah.

402
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,860
Short sleeves would present a problem.

403
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,400
The design's pretty sick, though.

404
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:53,720
Now you know.

405
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:54,340
Hmm.

406
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,620
Holy shit.

407
00:16:56,340 --> 00:17:00,820
I totally had you pinned for the weird, gloomy otaku type, but you're full of surprises,

408
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,300
aren't you?

409
00:17:01,660 --> 00:17:04,700
Otaku type, no, but everything else describes me to a T.

410
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:08,960
Now that I'm getting a good look, he's kinda handsome.

411
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:10,540
His hair still sucks, though.

412
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:12,680
So, is P.E. in the gym today?

413
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,980
Is this the kind of face what he's attracted to?

414
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:17,040
That's my head!

415
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,260
No way!

416
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:20,000
You have a crap ton of piercings, too!

417
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,520
Okay, next.

418
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:27,040
You're one strange dude, you know that?

419
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:29,900
Why could ink or pierce if you're just gonna end up hiding it all?

420
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:34,960
Uh, have you ever done something completely on impulse?

421
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:36,140
It's not those things.

422
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:38,760
Your secret's safe with me.

423
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:44,340
Though, one thing I still want to know is how you and Hori magically became besties overnight.

424
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:48,860
It wasn't magic.

425
00:17:49,220 --> 00:17:50,720
It actually started a while back.

426
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:55,080
Although, the vibe I get is she's just being nice to me.

427
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:57,600
We're only friends, so there's nothing for you to worry about.

428
00:17:58,880 --> 00:17:59,280
Cool.

429
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:03,160
So, you won't mind if I ask her out?

430
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:04,180
Come on, man.

431
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:06,380
You don't need my permission for something like that.

432
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:07,320
Guess not.

433
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,020
Just felt right.

434
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,700
That ball's in Hori's court.

435
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:11,820
It's not my place.

436
00:18:11,820 --> 00:18:21,400
You skipped P.E., slacker!

437
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,320
And you had new duty, too!

438
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:25,300
So guess who got stuck cleaning up your mess?

439
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:25,760
Please!

440
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,240
I said I'm sorry!

441
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:28,560
Sorry doesn't cut it!

442
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:29,900
What do you want from me, then?

443
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,200
You were hanging out with Toru?

444
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:32,980
Look at you making friends.

445
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:33,820
Not really.

446
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,540
We were just talking.

447
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:40,320
Okay, what's with the cold shoulder?

448
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,240
Uh, what cold shoulder?

449
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,900
The one you're giving me as we speak.

450
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,300
I'm actually hot, not cold.

451
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:47,300
Did I accidentally offend you somehow?

452
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:49,120
Will you please just get off my back and my shoulders?

453
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:49,700
Hori.

454
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,340
I need to talk to you.

455
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:54,200
Privately.

456
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,560
I'll find you after school.

457
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,540
Well, I...

458
00:18:57,540 --> 00:18:59,280
Hold on!

459
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:00,120
No worries.

460
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,500
I can pick up Sota for you.

461
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:03,680
You see what he has to say.

462
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,620
It sounds like it might be important.

463
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:06,160
Huh?

464
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,160
But...

465
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:29,820
Sissy's home!

466
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:36,360
If the two of them wind up dating, I'll be a giant third wheel.

467
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:37,820
Sorry I'm late, Sota.

468
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,800
I'll get dinner started in a little bit.

469
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:41,720
Okay, sounds good.

470
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:46,660
Welcome home.

471
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,620
We need to talk.

472
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:53,700
If she says I have to stop coming over, then that's that.

473
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:55,980
I spoke with Toru.

474
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:56,880
Oh.

475
00:19:56,880 --> 00:20:02,380
He told me, you don't think you and I'd make a good match.

476
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:03,960
What?

477
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:05,800
Now I know what you really think.

478
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:08,240
All of this is just me being nice?

479
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,980
That's the kind of vibe you get?

480
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:12,860
Wait, didn't he tell you something else?

481
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,420
We're talking about you and me right now, not him.

482
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,180
So you said that?

483
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,040
Admit it to my face!

484
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:25,580
Yeah, I did.

485
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:28,440
So, you've been thinking this all along?

486
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:31,380
Every single second of every single day you came here?

487
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:31,980
No!

488
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,040
It's just...

489
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:36,000
I'm boring and depressing.

490
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:38,400
I put the most emo emo kit to shame.

491
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,140
How could I not be bothering you?

492
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,360
Or ruining your rep just by being around you?

493
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:43,360
You...

494
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,520
You wouldn't fight me here.

495
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:46,540
But some days I don't understand why.

496
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:49,820
Uh, Hori, don't cry!

497
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:50,840
Why?

498
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:52,220
You idiot!

499
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:55,600
Why should you have to worry about my reputation?

500
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:59,160
Don't assume stuff without even asking!

501
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:02,780
You better not say things like that ever again, dummy!

502
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:04,180
Sorry.

503
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,000
Really.

504
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:05,860
I am.

505
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:09,420
Just thinking about what you said...

506
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:10,940
Makes me so mad!

507
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,320
Um, let's take a breather.

508
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:16,780
If you ever stopped coming to my house...

509
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:20,100
Who would be around to wake me up when I fall asleep watching movies?

510
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,120
Who'd eat your portion of dinner?

511
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:22,840
Hori...

512
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:24,440
I'd have a fridge full of leftovers!

513
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:30,120
Toru?

514
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:32,860
He asked, but I turned him down.

515
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:33,160
Really?

516
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:35,180
But he seems like a genuinely sweet guy.

517
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:36,160
Um, what?

518
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:37,920
Did you just call another guy sweet?

519
00:21:38,300 --> 00:21:40,120
Toru might not be the only one with a crush.

520
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,540
Why not ask him out?

521
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:42,620
No thanks.

522
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:45,700
I don't think we'd get very far as a couple in the long run.

523
00:21:45,840 --> 00:21:46,280
Wait, what?

524
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:47,740
least if then.

525
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:56,680
Wait there.

526
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:59,360
First time to.

527
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:07,520
夢を見たんだ月が綺麗な夜に

528
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:19,580
また明日ねと手を振る君の姿が名残惜しくて

529
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:26,760
長袖のシャツに見覚えある道

530
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:31,760
少し寂しそうに見えた

531
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:38,760
胸が苦しくなるけど暖かい

532
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:44,760
気づいた冬の朝だ

533
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:50,760
約束するよ

534
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:57,760
近くにいるから見えない物事

535
00:22:57,760 --> 00:23:02,760
大事にするよ

536
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:07,760
言葉にできないんだけどね

537
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:17,760
暖かい

538
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:19,760
暖かい

539
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,760
暖かい

540
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:28,760
眩く者だ

541
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,760
どんなに会いない

542
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:33,760
ちょうどい

543
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:37,760
大事playing

544
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,760
何autre guest

545
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:41,760
少し難しい

546
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:46,760
お 노래をお願いします

547
00:23:46,760 --> 00:24:16,740
Thank you.

